From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:54:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: learn the swap_pace floor from
 unspaced swaps only

swap_pace aims a held internal-panel swap at the first 120 Hz grid tick
that is at least its lead ahead, and by default the lead is the shortest
start-to-completion time of recent swaps that were neither held nor
taken for video.

The panel shows frames at least two 4.17 ms ticks apart. A swap started
less than two ticks after the previous completion therefore completes
on that second tick however soon the firmware is done with it, and its
start-to-completion time is the rest of the spacing, not the firmware's
floor. Browsers playing video fullscreen mix 120 Hz bursts of such swaps
(player controls, the exit hint) into the video frames. On the J604 a
window of them raised the learned floor from 0.26 to 1.75 ms during one
fullscreen 1080p60 YouTube run. With that lead, video frames arriving
later than 1.33 ticks after a completion were aimed one grid tick late,
and held ones started early enough to make the odd tick before the aim:
17 to 30 % of the frames went off cadence, against about 1 % windowed.

Learn only from swaps that started at least two ticks after the
previous completion.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 3093e34c87..4164aeba2b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1789,7 +1789,7 @@ static bool dcp_m4_int_late_d590(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r, u32 id)
 static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 {
 	u64 start = READ_ONCE(r->int_start_cnt), done = READ_ONCE(r->int_done_cnt), lat;
-	u64 e = READ_ONCE(r->pace_e);
+	u64 e = READ_ONCE(r->pace_e), prev = r->int_prev_done;
 
 	if (r->int_prev_done && done > r->int_prev_done) {
 		/*
@@ -1831,6 +1831,19 @@ static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	 */
 	if (r->int_held || r->int_gated)
 		return;
+	/*
+	 * Nor from swaps started less than two ticks after the previous
+	 * completion: the panel shows frames at least two ticks apart, so such
+	 * a swap completes on that second tick however soon the firmware is
+	 * done, and its start-to-completion time is the rest of the spacing.
+	 * Fullscreen video in a browser mixes 120 Hz bursts of such swaps
+	 * (controls, the exit hint) into the video, and a window of them
+	 * raised the estimate from 0.26 to 1.75 ms (measured), which aimed
+	 * the next video frames a grid tick late and made held ones land a tick
+	 * before the aim.
+	 */
+	if (prev && start < prev + div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq(), 120))
+		return;
 	lat = done - start;
 	if (!r->int_lat_n || lat < r->int_lat_win)
 		r->int_lat_win = lat;
